# Exactly one ACTIVE owner invariant

```yaml
id: OWNER-CARDINALITY-INVARIANT
version: "2026-08-20"
status: LOCKED
phase: P1.3-B
authority: users-rbac.policy.ts · users.service.ts · invites.service.ts
decisions: [DEC-P9-015, DEC-P9-018, DEC-P9-019]
related:
  - subphases/9.4-users-rbac.md
  - users-api-dispatch-addendum.md
  - invite-accept-membership-invariant.mdoc
```

## Locked product rule

Every tenant/workspace has **exactly one ACTIVE owner**.

**Owner** is not role-alone:

```text
isActiveOwner ⇔ role = owner AND status = ACTIVE
```

Suspended `role=owner` rows are **not** owners for cardinality. Zero ACTIVE owners is invalid (except the documented provision bootstrap window, which `evaluateOwnerCreate` allows). Multiple ACTIVE owners is invalid.

## Policy location

Pure functions in `apps/api/src/identity/users-rbac.policy.ts`. Callers (P1.3-B):

| Mutation | Service | Policy |
| -------- | ------- | ------ |
| PATCH role | `patchWorkspaceUserRoleCore` | `evaluateOwnerRoleChange` then rank |
| DELETE member | `removeWorkspaceUser` | `evaluateOwnerMembershipRemoval` then rank |
| PATCH suspend | `suspendWorkspaceUserCore` | `evaluateOwnerMembershipSuspend` then rank |
| Ownership transfer | `transferWorkspaceOwnership` | `evaluateOwnershipTransfer` then repo |
| Invite accept (`role=owner`) | `acceptWorkspaceInvite` | `evaluateOwnerCreate` after join-only check |
| Bulk role / remove / suspend | same cores | no parallel checks |

## Repository boundary

- **Service-enforced** for PATCH / remove / suspend (directory always goes through `users.service`). Repo `updateMembershipRole` / `removeMembership` / `updateMembershipStatus` stay thin — no duplicated policy copy.
- **Transfer** repo keeps structural checks (membership exists, target ACTIVE); **cardinality** is decided in service via `evaluateOwnershipTransfer` before persist.
- **Owner invite accept:** service calls `evaluateOwnerCreate`; `acceptPendingInvite` also re-checks when `invite.role === owner` (write-boundary race guard, same policy function — not a second ruleset).

## Non-goals (P1.3-B)

- No Prisma migration / partial unique index (later).
- No UI / route / HTTP contract changes.
- No parallel RBAC module.

## Decision table

| Action | Allow | Reject | Code (existing vocabulary) |
| ------ | ----- | ------ | -------------------------- |
| PATCH role when target is ACTIVE owner | never (transfer only) | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| PATCH role when target `role=owner` (any status) | never | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| Remove ACTIVE owner | never | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| Remove when remaining ACTIVE owners would be 0 | never | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| Suspend ACTIVE owner | never | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| Suspend when remaining ACTIVE owners would be 0 | never | always | `RBAC_PROTECTED_ROLE_MODIFICATION_FORBIDDEN` |
| Create owner, `activeOwnerCount = 0` | bootstrap | — | — |
| Create owner, `activeOwnerCount ≥ 1` | never | always | `RBAC_OWNER_ROLE_ASSIGNMENT_FORBIDDEN` |
| Transfer | actor is the unique ACTIVE owner; target exists, ACTIVE, not that owner | otherwise | `OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER_FORBIDDEN` / `OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER_TARGET_INVALID` |

### Transfer result (when ok)

```text
actor  : owner + ACTIVE  →  admin + ACTIVE
target : (any non-owner role) + ACTIVE  →  owner + ACTIVE
ACTIVE owner count after = 1
```

Transfer is rejected when `activeOwnerUserIds` is not exactly `[actorUserId]` — extras would remain owner after the swap, violating exactly-one.

## Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant S as users.service / invites.service
  participant P as users-rbac.policy
  participant R as IdentityRepository
  S->>R: load memberships (role + status) for tenant
  S->>P: evaluateOwner*
  alt reject
    P-->>S: coded failure
  else allow
    S->>R: persist
  end
```
